    "created_at": "2016-11-09T20:36:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-09T20:36:37Z",
    "body": "I think for the vast majority of people reading the spec, they are following links either from the spec itself or from elsewhere, rather than intentionally typing `/multipage/#the-foo-element` and letting the script redirect. So they may almost never need the script to redirect anything. Yet everyone gets the overhead or downloading the big file, which can take a while on slow networks.\n\nI think an extra HTTP request is not a big deal in comparison, but if we want to improve that I suggest we look into using HTTP/2 where extra requests are not a problem AIUI.\n",
